  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive emergency response for Older People affected by Tropical Storm Chalane.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(ii) Sector 2: Food Security and Livelihood- Targeted Tropical storm Chalane Affected older people and PwDs have restored their food security and have their livelihood systems strengthened.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(iii) Sector 3: Shelter- increased security and safety of older people and people with disabilities in temporary shelters through the provision of shelter NFIs and construction of houses</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(iv) Sector 4: Policy and Protection Sector - Increased protection and inclusion for older women and men and older people with disabilities in the tropical storm Chalane affected population through awareness raising on GBV, SEA, ACHS and establishment of complaints and feedback mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By the end of the project, will have achieved the following results,                                                                                  
(i) Sector 1: Health- Enhanced local health system by increasing accessibility for older women and men and older people with disabilities to age friendly health services in order to reduce local transmission of covid-19 in resettlement areas that may be exacerbated by the influx of IDPs caused by the effects of tropical storm Chalane.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will predominantly target older women and men (60+), including older people with disabilities and their care givers. The project shall target 2500 HHs in Dondo and Muanza Districts of Sofala provinces. In Dondo we will work in Savane Resettlement and Mutua Resettlement Sites. In Muanza District we will work in Nhantsato, and Muanza Sede, sites which have been severely affected by the tropical storm.</narrative>
  </description>
